{"title":"2020 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Concise)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Concise)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Reverse_Order)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Reverse Order)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_CRITICALLY_THINK!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO CRITICALLY THINK!!!)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many distinguishable arrangements are there of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> brown tile, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> purple tile, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> green tiles, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yellow tiles in a row from left to right? (Tiles of the same color are indistinguishable.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/c/37c42896d5b7705f9701bba55b6239beca69df7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 210 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 420 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\  630 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 840 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1050$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"448\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's first find how many possibilities there would be if they were all distinguishable, then divide out the ones we overcounted.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce11f9bca5e74ba532323e045b62e2793d120b7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> ways to order <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> objects. However, since there's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3920c5e3f6b2e5749cd75c3853b63ae714d00561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> ways to switch the yellow tiles around without changing anything (since they're indistinguishable) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/46377b53287d0b7f76190da9e05acbd0fdedd334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2!=2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> ways to order the green tiles, we have to divide out these possibilities: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/d/8fd4e87be76d2bb89f666262d59e474f6a77e7da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7!}{3! \\cdot2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }420}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"138\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>~quacker88\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639c2626791167028adcf82c3a7aa800d810fce8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{7}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> ways to arrange the yellow tiles which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\nThen from the remaining tiles there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c9b68a04fadb4cbe90954c537de424c1519ef51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{4}{2}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" /> ways to arrange the green tiles.\nAnd now from the remaining two tiles and two slots we can see there are two ways to arrange the purple and brown tiles,\ngiving us an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8b540c814c67a468bf08a6ba8f2b34e6394f36f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35\\cdot6\\cdot2=420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~noahdavid (Edited by starshooter11)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can choose a different frame to solve this problem. Our tile combination can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2c72015d290b051926efbdcacc787f917e6ca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y, Y, Y, G, G, B, P.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> We can focus on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/9/c69d85278ac6299c9ac487c6a10026a6a3546dd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y, Y, Y, G, G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> first, which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/4390223acc5001312b7775e3f7b64511943810a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{5}{3}=10.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"83\" height=\"53\" /> Now we can insert our brown tile into this which only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices(like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aadd869424eec757bd71259bbe9e0ae07e7b11d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y,B, Y, Y, G, G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/8/828f86a8cdf037faa960e0d733b7f47c2eb0029d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y, Y, Y, G, G, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /> etc.), then insert purple tile which only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices(like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e401adc3bd3e9ae26522c3193c658ff779a8ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B,Y, P, Y, Y, G, G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744cd080c529d6e4ac8c9f045cd1e268810efee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B, Y, Y, Y, G, G, P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /> etc.). Multiply them together we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/285ab492c3d7f52733dc250b147c301d0131432a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\cdot 6\\cdot 7=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 420}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"161\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~@azure123456 BZ\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Concise.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Concise)\">Solution 4 (Concise)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Concise)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be brown, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be purple, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be green, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be yellow. Then, we are just ordering <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4585f26aeb8e8141925544a7807545c4fd9b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7!}{3! \\cdot 2!} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 420}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>~MrThinker\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Reverse_Order.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Reverse_Order)\">Solution 5 (Reverse Order)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Reverse Order)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d01e31e95bfbbd79b15b6cdcaf416e20585c691e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 1 + 2 + 3 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" /> ways you can arrange the brown tile, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/aba943173cf5e981d32e9caa2b2a41dd5ef43148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> ways you can arrange the purple tile, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bfd1a7ef429b76abe80e3bf7e963b1bc1dc742f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{5}{2} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" /> ways to arrange the green tiles, and only 1 possible arrangement of the yellow tiles after all of this. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b17ae950bd6d0395b650dcbba6a61c5965cb2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 * 6 * 10 * 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 420}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"196\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ RealJohnMantle\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_CRITICALLY_THINK.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_CRITICALLY_THINK!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO CRITICALLY THINK!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO CRITICALLY THINK!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SQ8XRpl2gXE\">https://youtu.be/SQ8XRpl2gXE</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0W3VmFp55cM?t=540\">https://youtu.be/0W3VmFp55cM?t=540</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Gkm5rU5MlOU\">https://youtu.be/Gkm5rU5MlOU</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline